# Deploy-safety FLOOR — framework-native gate primitives (Sub-cycle A) — apply ladder

Per `docs/plans/deploy-safety-floor-gate-primitives.md` — implements
Sub-cycle A of the always-on safety FLOOR for loam's productionizing
capability: the framework-native PreToolUse gate primitives every higher
(opt-in) deploy tier composes on top of, and that no marketplace toggle
casually turns off.

Scope (plan §6 Sub-cycle A): NEW component
`framework/deploy-safety-floor/`.

  - AC.DSF.1 — per-environment config abstraction: an inert, owner-editable
    `deploy.yaml` / `.loam/environments.yaml` (is_production / tier /
    reversible / gate / security_profile / immutable id) that parses into a
    typed model; an invalid tier or a missing is_production is rejected at
    load (fail-CLOSED load). Policy in YAML; enforcement in the hook.
  - AC.DSF.2 — destructive-action classifier keyed off the RESOLVED target;
    gate strength = max(declared protection, resolved-target
    production-ness). A destructive command resolving to a declared-prod
    identity is prod-gated even when the active env is declared non-prod
    (closes G2's config-resolvable cases).
  - AC.DSF.3 — rename-safety preserved: gate height derives from structured
    fields (is_production / tier), never the environment name.
  - AC.DSF.4 — write-time prod-string block: a prod-shaped connection
    string (matching a declared-prod identity) written into a
    non-prod / local config file is blocked at write time; the secret value
    is never echoed into the reply, brief, or log.
  - AC.DSF.6 — attestation-record contract + refuse-all-destructive default
    (framework-side half of F-0/G1): an is_production / tier real-infra env
    with no fresh attestation record refuses every destructive verb and
    says, in plain words, it is not yet protected. The live provider PROBES
    that populate the record are deploy-tier (OUT of scope per plan §3
    HALT-2); the DEFAULT POSTURE + refusal are in scope and enforced here.
  - AC.DSF.7 ★ (outcome-altitude) — the REAL floor PreToolUse hook
    entry-point over raw stdin with NO pre-arranged state: a fabricated
    destructive command in an is_production context with no attestation
    returns a deny naming the target + sub-action in non-technical words,
    and the same entry-point still returns deny (fail-CLOSED) when its
    evaluation raises (corrupt attestations file). The floor's destructive
    path fails CLOSED, inverting the advisory D-SECHK.FAIL-OPEN convention
    for that path only.
  - AC.COV.1 — the new floor guard FM.DESTRUCTIVE-PROD-UNGATED is catalogued
    in `framework/protection-matrix/data/failure-mode-guard-matrix.yaml`
    (default_on: YES, class: floor, resolvable guard_ref) and the generated
    companion `docs/design/protection-matrix.md` is regenerated; `loam
    guards` reports it covered (`[ok]`), no divergence, no new floor gap.

Lens 1 (compose, don't re-derive): the classifier maps onto safety-layer's
`FrameworkFloorCategory` (destroy_user_data_beyond_workspace /
modify_production_systems_serving_real_users) rather than minting its own
action-class enum. The gate is a deterministic `command` PreToolUse hook —
the floor must not be probabilistic; never an LLM-judge gate.

Method-level choices are the builder's call per ODD §1.1; the plan fixed
the ACs (§5), the named decisions (A–E + HALT-2 split), the fence (§2/§6),
and the halt triggers (§8), not the implementation.

